hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21030","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, he said: Ubadah ibn Qurt said: you commit things that are finer in your eyes than hair, we used to count them in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among the deadly sins. He said: then they mentioned that to Muhammad, he said, and he said: he spoke the truth, I see dragging the lower garment among them."
"21031","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu Qatadah, from Ubadah ibn Qurt or Qurs, he said: you do deeds that are finer in your eyes than hair, we used to count them in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among the deadly sins."
"21032","Affan narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, Abu Qatadah narrated to us, from Ubadah ibn Qurs or Qurt: you today do deeds that are finer in your eyes than hair, we used to count them in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among the deadly sins. So I said to Abu Qatadah: what if he had lived to our time? Then Abu Qatadah said: he would have said that even more."
